---
import Base from "../../layouts/Base.astro";
import Section from "../../components/Section.astro";
import Stage from "../../components/Stage.astro";
---
<Base title="Breadcrumb: an accessible trail" description="iVOLT breadcrumb: an ordered list of links inside a labelled nav, with a CSS separator and aria-current on the last item. CSS only.">
  <article class="docs-prose" data-enriched>
    <h1>Breadcrumb</h1>
    <p>Shows where the current page sits in the site hierarchy. The separator is drawn with CSS so screen readers only read the links.</p>
    <p class="docs-meta"><strong>CSS:</strong> <code>css/components/breadcrumb.css</code> (in <code>ivolt.css</code>).</p>
    <Stage primary name="breadcrumb/basic" title="A trail with the current page" />

    <Section title="Markup" num={1}>
      <p><code>nav.iv-breadcrumb[aria-label="Breadcrumb"]</code> → <code>ol.iv-breadcrumb__list</code> → <code>li.iv-breadcrumb__item</code>. The last item carries <code>aria-current="page"</code> and is not a link.</p>
    </Section>

    <Section title="Common mistakes" num={2}>
      <ul><li>Separator characters typed into the HTML (they get read aloud).</li><li>Linking the current page to itself.</li></ul>
    </Section>
    <Section title="Full example" num={3}>
      <p>The trail is an ordered list, because the order is the meaning. The <code>nav</code> gets its own name so it can be told apart from the main navigation in the landmarks list of a screen reader.</p><pre tabindex="0"><code>&lt;nav class="iv-breadcrumb" aria-label="Breadcrumb"&gt;
  &lt;ol class="iv-breadcrumb__list"&gt;
    &lt;li class="iv-breadcrumb__item"&gt;&lt;a href="/"&gt;Home&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
    &lt;li class="iv-breadcrumb__item"&gt;&lt;a href="/docs"&gt;Docs&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
    &lt;li class="iv-breadcrumb__item" aria-current="page"&gt;Breadcrumb&lt;/li&gt;
  &lt;/ol&gt;
&lt;/nav&gt;</code></pre>
    </Section>

    <Section title="How the separator works" num={4}>
      <p>The separator is a masked inline SVG on <code>::before</code>, never a character in the HTML, so it is not announced and it takes the text colour of the theme through <code>currentColor</code>. It is drawn only between items (adjacent-sibling selector). The list wraps onto several lines on a narrow screen instead of scrolling sideways.</p><p>Locals: <code>--iv-breadcrumb-gap</code> (space around the separator) and <code>--iv-breadcrumb-separator-size</code>.</p>
    </Section>

    <Section title="Search engines" num={5}>
      <p>The visible trail does not tell a search engine about your hierarchy on its own. If you want breadcrumbs in search results, add a <code>BreadcrumbList</code> in JSON-LD with the same items; this site does exactly that on every documentation page.</p>
    </Section>
  </article>
</Base>
